WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.000
MODULE: A module groups related Python code. Often it is a .py file; built-in and extension modules also exist.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:28.000
PACKAGE: A package is a module that can contain submodules. A regular package usually has __init__.py; namespace packages can omit it.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:42.000
LIBRARY: A library is reusable code, often made of modules and packages. lib is a common abbreviation, not a special Python keyword.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:56.000
FRAMEWORK: A framework supplies an application structure and runs parts of the workflow. Your code fits into that structure, for example Django views.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:10.000
CONNECT THE IDEAS: Modules and packages describe code organization. Libraries and frameworks describe how reusable code is used. These labels can overlap.
